"""Research narrative driven by the canonical reconstruction outputs."""
import csv,json
from pathlib import Path
ROOT=Path(__file__).resolve().parents[1]
def load():return json.loads((ROOT/'results/rental-market-analysis.json').read_text(encoding='utf8'))
def money(v):return f'EUR {v:,.2f}'
def chapter(p,h,sub,page,table,fig):
    r=load();c=r['counts'];ps=r['primary'];e=r['evidence_informed_scenario'];h0=r['historical_900_scenario']
    rows=list(csv.DictReader((ROOT/'data/rental/primary-comparable-sample.csv').open(encoding='utf8')))
    h('4 The long-term rental comparison')
    p(f"The rental evidence was reconstructed through a Manual online rental listing review on 14 October 2026. The {c['total_candidates']} candidate rows contain the original 21 records, 20 preliminary leads and {c['additional_candidates']} additional advertisements actually investigated. These input sets overlap. They do not establish {c['total_candidates']} independent apartments. Source content, contract terms and base prices were checked where accessible, with unresolved leads retained in the audit.")
    p(f"The strict selected sample contains {ps['n']} distinct comparable advertisement-based property groups, with arithmetic mean {money(ps['mean'])} per month and median {money(ps['median'])}. Its recorded base rents sum to {money(ps['total'])}. The target of 20 primary properties was not reached. This is a convenience sample of source-verified offers, not a representative city rent or a confirmation that all apartments remain available. The historical EUR 900 model is retained separately.")
    sub('Study scope and comparable-property criteria')
    p("The operational selection uses Comune di Bergamo advertisements labelled Centro or Sant'Alessandro, or explicitly located at Piazzetta Santo Spirito. These are source-defined central urban labels, not an official polygon or an invented radius. Stazione, San Paolo, Canovine, Borgo Palazzo and other labels alone are outside this selected scope. Source labels can differ across portals and do not replace property-level geocoding. OMI B2 is used only as an external reference; the sample is not claimed to occupy that single zone.")
    table(['Primary criterion','Rule'],[['Property','Entire furnished apartment; two rooms and one bedroom'],['Size','40–65 advertised m² inclusive'],['Contract','Explicit ordinary 4+4; a documented 4+4 option may qualify'],['Price','Monthly base asking rent; separately billed charges excluded'],['Evidence','Source details reviewed; no unresolved identity or material feature/price conflict']])
    p("A separate secondary cohort retains central furnished one-bedroom offers of 40–80 advertised m² with larger size or annual/free/unspecified ordinary residential duration. Temporary and serviced offers, inaccessible historical-only records and material contradictions do not enter either cohort. The geographic and size criteria were not loosened to reach the target. The data dictionary and source register document every decision. [R01–R03]")
    page();sub('Candidate reconciliation and property identity')
    table(['Stage','Count and interpretation'],[['Original / preliminary / additional rows',f"21 / 20 / {c['additional_candidates']}"],['Total rows / distinct source URLs',f"{c['total_candidates']} / {c['distinct_source_urls']}"],['Confirmed duplicate clusters / rows removed',f"{c['confirmed_duplicate_clusters']} / {c['confirmed_duplicate_rows_removed']}"],['Canonical groups including unresolved identities',str(c['canonical_groups_including_unresolved'])],['Probable duplicate review pairs',str(c['probable_duplicate_review_pairs'])],['Primary / secondary properties',f"{c['primary_properties']} / {c['secondary_properties']}"],['Excluded canonical groups including unresolved',str(c['excluded_canonical_groups'])],['Unresolved candidate rows',str(c['unresolved_candidate_rows'])],['Total independent physical apartments','Unknown for unresolved leads and probable matches']])
    p("Exact URL repeats merge input rows. Different URLs merge only after a reviewed match using distinctive description, floor, size, contract and advertiser signals. Torquato Tasso 75 is the same recovered advertisement in C13 and A05. Sant'Orsola 25 is a confirmed cross-platform apartment match, but its EUR 850 and EUR 900 headlines disagree, so the cluster is excluded rather than selecting a preferred price. Canonical groups include provisional identities and are not a verified physical-property census.")
    p("Borfuro 9 remains a probable cross-platform match: distinctive annual-renewable wording, second floor and EUR 110 charges agree, but 50/55 m² and EUR 1,200/1,000 disagree. Two third-floor Camozzi offers may differ only by a EUR 150 parking option; both are excluded pending unit confirmation. Conversely, Zambianchi 2 versus 3 and Sant'Orsola 2 versus 25 have different civic numbers and property attributes. The old Quarenghi/Borfuro price overlap did not justify treating them as a duplicate. [R03]")
    p(f"Origin reconciliation: two original properties and two newly eligible preliminary leads contribute to the primary cohort, alongside {c['primary_origins'].get('additional_discovery',0)} additional properties. A05 overlaps the original C13 and does not add a new apartment. The source registry retains all original links and the six unresolved exact-URL leads.")
    fig('candidate-screening.png','Figure 6 Candidate reconciliation and screening','Stage counts describe different sets and are not additive. Canonical groups include unresolved identities; they are not a physical-property total. Source: candidate registry and reviewed identity decisions.')
    page();sub('Price normalisation and research corrections')
    p("The original CSV is unchanged: 17 recorded numeric rents total EUR 17,240 and have descriptive mean EUR 1,014.12, while four prices remain missing in that historical snapshot. The 20 preliminary lead prices total EUR 17,185 and average EUR 859.25. Neither raw statistic describes 20 or 21 independently verified comparable properties. Four historical missing prices were recovered as new observations: Broseta 10 EUR 1,300, Moroni 237 EUR 1,000, Paleocapa EUR 700 and Mazzini 24 EUR 1,300. All four remain outside the primary cohort by contract, property or location criteria.")
    p("At Broseta 44, the retrieved source advertises a EUR 900 package including utilities and condominium, alongside a separate EUR 120 condominium field. It does not corroborate the proposed EUR 590 base plus EUR 120 charges plus EUR 190 services split. No base rent is inferred and the transitory offer is excluded. At Pignolo 23, the source explicitly distinguishes EUR 850 base rent and EUR 50 reimbursement, EUR 900 total. The EUR 850 headline is already base rent and is not reduced again. Deposits, optional garages and tenant-billed charges do not become owner rent. [R02]")
    p("A supplied Cucchi bilocale link now displays a studio near Piazza Sant'Anna, so it does not verify A03. Partigiani 4 conflicts with Torretta 10 in the same advertisement. One central offer's narrative says furnished one-bedroom while its structured fields say unfurnished and zero bedrooms. These contradictions are recorded and excluded. Expired advertisements and older search-cache details remain in the audit without being relabelled as current comparables.")
    sub('Primary and secondary rental statistics')
    table(['Measure','Primary','Secondary'],[['Property count',str(ps['n']),str(r['secondary']['n'])],['Arithmetic mean / month',money(ps['mean']),money(r['secondary']['mean'])],['Median / month',money(ps['median']),money(r['secondary']['median'])],['Sample standard deviation',money(ps['sd']),money(r['secondary']['sd'])],['Minimum / maximum',f"{money(ps['min'])} / {money(ps['max'])}",f"{money(r['secondary']['min'])} / {money(r['secondary']['max'])}"],['Quartiles Q1 / Q3',f"{money(ps['q1'])} / {money(ps['q3'])}",f"{money(r['secondary']['q1'])} / {money(r['secondary']['q3'])}"],['Interquartile range',money(ps['iqr']),money(r['secondary']['iqr'])]])
    p("Means use unrounded individual base rents, standard deviation uses n−1 and quartiles use inclusive linear interpolation. Secondary observations are not pooled into the primary mean. The historical six-record subgroup remains a separate snapshot with mean EUR 1,000 and median EUR 900; neither statistic is the new sample result.")
    page();sub('Rental distribution and comparable offers')
    fig('rent-distribution.png','Figure 7 Primary monthly base-rent distribution',f"{ps['n']} selected properties; mean {money(ps['mean'])}, median {money(ps['median'])}. The distribution shows sample dispersion, not population uncertainty or a representative market range. Source: primary-comparable-sample.csv.")
    table(['Property group','Location','Base EUR/month','Advertised m²'],[[x['property_id'],x['location'],f"{float(x['base_monthly_eur']):,.0f}",f"{float(x['advertised_m2']):g}"] for x in rows])
    p("These are public research identifiers. Source links, floors, charges and contract evidence are in the canonical registry and source register. Included garages, condition and floor differences remain. Some advertisements have old update dates; retrieval on the review date does not verify uninterrupted availability. No executed-rent panel, property inspection or advertiser confirmation was obtained.")
    page();sub('Independent benchmarks and measurement differences')
    fig('unit-price-context.png','Figure 8 Rental unit-price context','Primary values average individual base-rent/advertised-area ratios. Provider indicators cover different housing mixes and zone boundaries; the bars are contextual, not comparable property valuations. Benchmarks: September 2026 provider reports. OMI net-area ranges are stated separately.')
    p(f"The primary mean is {money(r['primary_price_per_advertised_m2']['mean'])} and median {money(r['primary_price_per_advertised_m2']['median'])} per advertised m² per month. Advertising areas may include weighted gardens, terraces or other accessories. These denominators differ from OMI's net-area basis. Source platform and contract counts are reproducible in rental-market-analysis.json; the primary contains 13 Immobiliare.it offers and one Subito offer, all with an explicit 4+4 branch.")
    table(['Source and period','Geography and rental metric'],[['Idealista September 2026','City EUR 14.20/m²; Centro Città EUR 14.90/m²'],['Immobiliare.it September 2026','City EUR 13.57/m²; combined Borgo Palazzo/Centro/Stazione EUR 14.31/m²'],['OMI 2025 second semester','B2 civil dwellings, normal: EUR 9.70–12.50 per net m²/month'],['OMI 2025 second semester','B2 civil dwellings, excellent: EUR 12.00–15.00 per net m²/month']])
    p("Idealista's July 2026 revision describes filtered and deduplicated advertisements, microzone medians and weighted geographic aggregation. Immobiliare's retrieved page reports broad residential averages without the detailed weighting specification. The previously suggested EUR 14.28 Centro value was not reproduced: the retrieved combined-zone value is EUR 14.31. These indicators are not the arithmetic mean of furnished bilocali. [R04–R06]")
    p("The official interactive OMI table displayed 2025/2 for Bergamo A794 zone B2, Centrale Via Verdi/Via dei Partigiani/Via Tasso. Its semiannual condition-specific ranges are not September–October 2026 asking-rent indices or a valuation of the sampled apartments. They are not multiplied by a chosen size to replace the sample rent. The source-register benchmark links and data dictionary preserve period, property category, methodology and surface basis. [R07]")
    page();sub('Historical and evidence-informed financial scenarios')
    p(f"The evidence-informed illustration uses the new primary arithmetic mean {money(ps['mean'])}, carried at full precision, and preserves every other model input. LTR net = 12 × monthly base rent × (1 − 0.21) − 1,800. It assumes 12 paid months and eligible tax, not observed vacancy-free income. No monetary owner-time deduction, financing or acquisition costs are introduced.")
    table(['Annual measure','Historical EUR900 rent','Sample-mean illustration'],[['Monthly base rent',money(900),money(ps['mean'])],['LTR gross',money(h0['annual_gross']),money(e['annual_gross'])],['LTR net',money(h0['ltr_net']),money(e['ltr_net'])],['STR net',money(h0['str_net']),money(e['str_net'])],['STR minus LTR',money(h0['gap']),money(e['gap'])]])
    fig('net-cash-comparison.png','Figure 9 Annual net cash by scenario','Same tax, expense and booking assumptions in both comparisons. Full-precision sample mean drives the new LTR calculation; rounding is for display only. These are conditional model outcomes, not realised property profits.')
    p(f"The new rent is only {money(900-ps['mean'])} below the historical assumption. LTR remains higher by {money(abs(e['gap']))} per year under the stated base. Such a small gap does not establish market superiority. At the new mean, eleven paid months reduce LTR net to {money(e['ltr_vacancy'][1]['ltr_net'])}; changing payment continuity alone can reverse the ranking.")
    page();sub('Updated sensitivity and break-even thresholds')
    fig('rent-sensitivity.png','Figure 10 Rent sensitivity and sample-mean scenario','Rent sensitivity isolates the rental alternative while STR stays at EUR 6,544.50. It does not predict attainable rent or occupancy. Source: shared financial formulas and canonical sample mean.')
    table(['STR additional fixed EUR/year','Historical gap','Sample-mean gap'],[[str(a['str_additional_fixed']),money(a['gap']),money(b['gap'])] for a,b in zip(h0['differential_cost_sensitivity'],e['differential_cost_sensitivity'])])
    p("Reducing STR-specific fixed costs raises STR relative cash; changing common costs equally for both strategies leaves the gap unchanged. Price, bookings and costs interact in practice, so these isolated tests are conditional. The existing EUR 100/115/130 nightly-price and 150/180/210 booked-night grid is preserved and compared against the new rental alternative in the results JSON.")
    page();sub('Conversion thresholds under the new rent')
    fig('break-even-comparison.png','Figure 11 Booked nights required by rental alternative','EUR 115 gross nightly revenue; incremental preparation recovered over five years. Required nights use ceiling, never conventional rounding. The graph states scenario requirements and does not forecast occupancy.')
    table(['Extra setup EUR','Historical nights','New nights','New price at180 nights'],[[f"{a['setup']:,}",str(a['minimum_whole_nights']),str(b['minimum_whole_nights']),money(b['required_nightly_price'])] for a,b in zip(h0['break_even'],e['break_even'])])
    p(f"Without extra setup, the new comparison requires {e['break_even'][0]['minimum_whole_nights']} booked nights at EUR 115, or {money(e['break_even'][0]['required_nightly_price'])} gross per night at 180 bookings. With EUR 15,000 additional preparation and five-year recovery, it requires {e['break_even'][-1]['minimum_whole_nights']} nights or {money(e['break_even'][-1]['required_nightly_price'])} at 180 bookings. The historical thresholds remain 184/203/222/241. A required surplus still has to be achievable in the same property.")
def appendix(p,h,sub,page,table):
    master=list(csv.DictReader((ROOT/'data/rental/master-listing-registry.csv').open(encoding='utf8')))
    page();h('Appendix B Complete rental candidate reconciliation')
    p('All supplied candidates and every additional advertisement investigated are retained below. Base EUR records a source-specific base price when identified, including explicitly labelled historical-index values; it does not imply cohort eligibility or current availability. P groups identify advertisement-based reviewed properties; U groups are unresolved. The exact URLs, locations, floor, contract, fees, recorded historical prices and detailed reasons remain in data/rental/master-listing-registry.csv and the complete linked Rental_Listing_Investigation.md table. No personal advertiser contacts are published.')
    for origin,title in [('original_21','Original C records'),('assistant_20','Preliminary A leads'),('additional_discovery','Additional N advertisements')]:
        sub(title)
        table(['Candidate','Group','Base EUR','m²','Contract','Disposition'],[[x['candidate_id'],x['property_id'],f"{float(x['base_monthly_eur']):,.0f}" if x['base_monthly_eur'] else 'Unknown',f"{float(x['advertised_m2']):g}" if x['advertised_m2'] else 'Unknown',x['contract'] or 'Unresolved',x['cohort']+'; '+x['status']] for x in master if x['origin']==origin])
